    "result_text": "Done. The change is implemented and the test suite is green.\n\n## What I did\n\nThe spec required exposing `checkDigit` \u2014 a single Luhn check digit computed over the digits of `customerCode`.\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `checkDigit` property to the `Owner` schema (readOnly integer, 0\u20139), so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a `@Mapping(target = \"checkDigit\", expression = \"java(checkDigit(owner))\")` on `toOwnerDto`, plus a `checkDigit(Owner)` helper that computes the Luhn check digit over the digits in `customerCode`. The algorithm mirrors the standard Luhn variant the acceptance test replicates (right-to-left, doubling the rightmost digit first, `(10 - sum % 10) % 10`), so the recomputed value matches exactly.\n\n## Result\n\n`./mvnw test` \u2192 **BUILD SUCCESS**, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` (the sole test, `AcceptanceTest.coreCheckDigitIsLuhnOfCustomerCode`, passes).",
